# ── Apple token revocation — the-bourbon-cup ────────────────────────
# Read by `revokeAppleToken` in index.js. See .env.example for what each value
# is and where it comes from; this is the filled-in copy the Firebase CLI
# uploads at deploy time.
#
# NONE OF THIS IS SECRET, which is why it is committed rather than sitting in
# a gitignored .env on one laptop: a key id travels in the JWT `kid` header, a
# team id is already in App.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj, and a bundle id is
# printed in the App Store. The one real secret is the .p8 itself, which goes
# to Google's secret manager and never here:
#
#   firebase functions:secrets:set APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY --data-file C:\dev\keys\AuthKey_<NEW_KEY_ID>.p8

# TODO — the key this pointed at is GONE.
#
# 9K7J7J2VGT was revoked on 10 Sep 2026 after its private key was pasted into a
# chat window: `functions:secrets:access` prints the key material, and the
# output went somewhere it could be read. Destroying the Secret Manager version
# does not un-issue a key, so the key itself had to be revoked at Apple.
#
# Use `functions:secrets:describe` to check a secret exists — it reports the
# versions and their state and prints no key.
#
# Fill in the id of the REPLACEMENT key. It is the filename Apple gives you,
# AuthKey_<APPLE_KEY_ID>.p8, and it is shown on the key's page once.
#
# Whatever the new key is, check "Sign in with Apple" is among the services on
# it. The APNs key on this project is a different one (7UA9A9SR3K,
# docs/app-store.md), and a key without that service ticked gets
# `invalid_client` back from Apple, which reads exactly like a malformed .p8.
# scripts/apple-key-check.mjs settles it.
APPLE_KEY_ID=

APPLE_TEAM_ID=7RRL56R755

# TODO — the only value not already known to this repo.
#
# The Services ID for the WEB sign-in flow: Apple Developer portal →
# Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles → Identifiers → filter to Services IDs.
# It is the one whose Sign in with Apple configuration lists
# https://the-bourbon-cup.firebaseapp.com/__/auth/handler as a return URL, and
# it is NOT com.thebourboncup.app — that is the App ID, and the two are
# separate registrations (docs/app-store.md §377).
#
# Left blank, a deletion from the WEBSITE logs failed-precondition and carries
# on; the iOS path is unaffected, since a native code is bound to the bundle id
# below rather than to this.
APPLE_CLIENT_ID=

# The iOS bundle id, used for a code from the native Apple sheet.
APPLE_BUNDLE_ID=com.thebourboncup.app
